            "review_title": "Review at Kutom Seafood Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Lương Thị Loan\nNghe An Province, Vietnam5 contributions\n0\n#haisan\nJul 2026 • Family\nKu Tom Da Nang Seafood (situated at 283-285 Ho Chi Minh, Son Tea District) is an ideal destination for those who love fresh seafood living in the tank. With an average price of just 49K for sauces, snacks, visitors can choose their own ingredients and enjoy the full taste of the sea right in the city center.\nLocated on the axis of Ho Chi Minh Road, the restaurant is just a few minutes from the American Beach, very convenient for visitors to combine bathing and eating. The cafeteria space is spacious, airy, provides a comfortable feeling and is suitable for gathering with family and friends after a day of play.\n\nKu Tom’s biggest plus is its large-scale fresh seafood reservoir system. Here, you can catch the seafood that are swimming with your own hands such as shrimp, crab, chickpeas, chickpeas,... Food prepared immediately after peeling should retain its natural sweetness, strong meat and not beaten. Ku Tom seafood is a worthy choice of rice bowl, a good balance between the criteria of \"sweet, filled, cheap\" and polite space. You can follow more promotional programs of the restaurant on the Fanpage of Ku Tom Da Nang Seafood before visiting.\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten July 22, 2026",
